Makes sense, agreed that reducer is overkill for the scope of this app.

I've had the token issue in the back of my mind but hadn't come up with the best way to solve it. Your
```javascript
export function getSession(){
  return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('session'))
}
```
suggestion is the simplest to implement and should work to allow the `api` to grab the token. The main concern here would be a possible performance hit caused by needing to `JSON.parse` the session object on every call. A better integrated design could be making the `api` part of the `AppContext` to give it direct access to the global state. But as long as you're ok with the quicker-to-implement `getSession` solution for this project I'll go with that.

Unless I'm missing something, I don't think I'll need `setSession`, I can just use `AppContext.setSession` everywhere.

