@alex-kovoy giving it some thought, I think it is the case that the only piece of fully application level state for this simple of an app is whether or not the user is authenticated. 

OTOH my intention here was to lay down a global state management system that would make the app more maintainable and easier to evolve in the long run, which in my experience is the type of pub-sub system I have here -- any component can "publish" a mutation to the global state, and then each component "subscribes" to pieces of the global state relevant to them, and automatically reacts to changes (basically the Mobx model).

Probably I should make that more clear though by not constraining my naming to be "session"-based, maybe just go back to calling it the more general "store"? Or do you still want me to change it to something closer to your example?

